WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.304
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A one.

2
00:00:05.604 --> 00:00:09.141
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.441 --> 00:00:15.948
Unit twenty-two: Ordinal Numbers and Dates. Today you will say the order of things and talk about dates.

4
00:00:16.248 --> 00:00:19.040
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.256
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.117 --> 00:00:24.839
First.

7
00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:27.710
First means number one in order.

8
00:00:28.317 --> 00:00:29.898
Today is the first day.

9
00:00:30.483 --> 00:00:32.613
Your turn. Say: First.

10
00:00:35.467 --> 00:00:36.410
First.

11
00:00:37.150 --> 00:00:38.023
Second.

12
00:00:39.017 --> 00:00:41.132
Second means number two in order.

13
00:00:41.717 --> 00:00:43.217
He is the second student.

14
00:00:43.817 --> 00:00:46.179
Your turn. Say: Second.

15
00:00:49.033 --> 00:00:49.837
Second.

16
00:00:50.583 --> 00:00:51.317
Third.

17
00:00:52.317 --> 00:00:54.363
Third means number three in order.

18
00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:56.381
She is third in line.

19
00:00:56.983 --> 00:00:59.949
Your turn. Say: Third.

20
00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:03.557
Third.

21
00:01:04.317 --> 00:01:05.016
Tenth.

22
00:01:06.017 --> 00:01:08.121
Tenth means number ten in order.

23
00:01:08.717 --> 00:01:10.345
My birthday is on the tenth.

24
00:01:10.950 --> 00:01:13.417
Your turn. Say: Tenth.

25
00:01:16.267 --> 00:01:16.989
Tenth.

26
00:01:17.750 --> 00:01:18.612
Twentieth.

27
00:01:19.617 --> 00:01:21.965
Twentieth means number twenty in order.

28
00:01:22.550 --> 00:01:24.317
It is the twentieth of May.

29
00:01:24.917 --> 00:01:27.836
Your turn. Say: Twentieth.

30
00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:31.562
Twentieth.

31
00:01:32.317 --> 00:01:33.062
Date.

32
00:01:34.050 --> 00:01:36.003
Date means the day, month and year.

33
00:01:36.617 --> 00:01:37.943
What is the date today?

34
00:01:38.550 --> 00:01:40.889
Your turn. Say: Date.

35
00:01:43.733 --> 00:01:44.479
Date.

36
00:01:45.217 --> 00:01:46.044
Birthday.

37
00:01:47.050 --> 00:01:49.514
Birthday means the day of the year when you were born.

38
00:01:50.117 --> 00:01:51.745
My birthday is in May.

39
00:01:52.350 --> 00:01:55.153
Your turn. Say: Birthday.

40
00:01:58.000 --> 00:01:59.001
Birthday.

41
00:01:59.750 --> 00:02:00.449
Month.

42
00:02:01.450 --> 00:02:03.914
Month means one of twelve parts of the year.

43
00:02:04.517 --> 00:02:05.854
May is the fifth month.

44
00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:08.626
Your turn. Say: Month.

45
00:02:11.467 --> 00:02:12.282
Month.

46
00:02:13.067 --> 00:02:17.031
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:17.883 --> 00:02:21.058
Visal, when is your birthday? Please say the date.

48
00:02:22.150 --> 00:02:33.257
It is on the tenth of May. We use ordinal numbers for dates and order: first, second, third, tenth, twentieth. Most ordinals end in th.

49
00:02:34.350 --> 00:02:35.920
Which ordinals are special?

50
00:02:37.017 --> 00:02:51.642
First, second and third are irregular. Then four becomes fourth, five becomes fifth, twelve becomes twelfth. For numbers like twenty, we change y to ie: twentieth.

51
00:02:52.750 --> 00:02:54.134
How do we write dates?

52
00:02:55.250 --> 00:03:06.206
In writing we use 5th May or May 5th. In speaking we say the fifth of May. We use on before a date: My birthday is on the tenth of May.

53
00:03:07.367 --> 00:03:09.436
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:10.283 --> 00:03:13.235
Grammar focus: Ordinal numbers and dates.

55
00:03:13.535 --> 00:03:14.710
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:15.417 --> 00:03:16.894
the first of January

57
00:03:17.783 --> 00:03:19.063
the tenth of May

58
00:03:19.950 --> 00:03:21.601
the twentieth of October

59
00:03:22.567 --> 00:03:30.504
Use ordinal numbers for order and dates: first, second, third, then add th. Say the fifth of May. Use on before a date.

60
00:03:31.250 --> 00:03:35.423
Be careful! Don't say: My birthday is the five of May.

61
00:03:37.367 --> 00:03:40.028
Say: My birthday is on the fifth of May.

62
00:03:40.328 --> 00:03:42.339
Use an ordinal number with on.

63
00:03:43.133 --> 00:03:45.693
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:46.500 --> 00:03:47.757
Important Dates.

65
00:03:48.057 --> 00:03:50.242
Today is the first day of the month.

66
00:03:51.233 --> 00:03:53.628
My birthday is on the tenth of May.

67
00:03:54.633 --> 00:03:56.865
The second month of the year is February.

68
00:03:57.867 --> 00:04:00.656
I am third in my class, and my friend is second.

69
00:04:01.667 --> 00:04:03.771
The twentieth of the month is a holiday.

70
00:04:04.867 --> 00:04:08.648
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:09.483 --> 00:04:11.715
The blank month of the year is January.

72
00:04:12.015 --> 00:04:14.902
A, one. B, first. C, oneth.

73
00:04:18.467 --> 00:04:20.571
The answer is B: first.

74
00:04:21.717 --> 00:04:24.381
She is the blank student in line. (3)

75
00:04:24.681 --> 00:04:27.730
A, three. B, third. C, threeth.

76
00:04:31.267 --> 00:04:32.953
The answer is B: third.

77
00:04:34.117 --> 00:04:35.803
We say 5th as the blank.

78
00:04:36.103 --> 00:04:39.222
A, five. B, fiveth. C, fifth.

79
00:04:42.767 --> 00:04:44.766
The answer is C: fifth.

80
00:04:45.917 --> 00:04:47.498
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:04:47.798 --> 00:04:54.784
A, My birthday is in the tenth of May.. B, My birthday is on the tenth of May.. C, My birthday is at the tenth of May..

82
00:04:58.333 --> 00:05:01.494
The answer is B: My birthday is on the tenth of May..

83
00:05:02.650 --> 00:05:05.602
According to the reading, which month is second?

84
00:05:05.902 --> 00:05:09.555
A, February. B, January. C, March.

85
00:05:13.100 --> 00:05:15.367
The answer is A: February.

86
00:05:16.567 --> 00:05:19.486
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:20.350 --> 00:05:21.827
When is your birthday?

88
00:05:30.617 --> 00:05:32.129
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:32.429 --> 00:05:46.894
My birthday is on the fifteenth of August. It is in the eighth month of the year. I use an ordinal number to say the date, and I say on before it. I like my birthday because I eat cake with my family.

90
00:05:47.194 --> 00:05:48.856
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:49.750 --> 00:05:54.179
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and ordinal numbers and dates.

92
00:05:54.479 --> 00:05:58.443
Today's value is gratitude. Say thank you for your home and family.

93
00:05:58.743 --> 00:06:02.231
See you in Unit twenty-three. Goodbye!

94
00:06:02.531 --> 00:06:04.893
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

